          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP 263 ravine drive Edmonton&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We decided to take the hard way by climbing through the trees instead of parking nearby thanks for another cap! &lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684558327">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-07T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3339080">Gimli*/GeoJoce</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP263 Edmonton (Ravine Drive)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Wow what a view!  I loved coming here and finding this one and taking it in.  The house next door had me a bit in awe as well.  :)  The cap was a sort of quick find....I finally got a hint in Coolcat's log.  That combined with the context pics and I had my eye on it.  I took my pics and was on to the next cap and view point.  TFTBC and for bringing me here!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="683763204">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-04T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="7458582">mkPerry</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP263 Edmonton (Ravine Drive)

Stopped for this while driving back to the office. The area is pretty quiet other than a number of house renovations going on. Find was quick and the numbers easily read. 

Thanks outforthehunt for another BCP. &lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="682022542">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-29T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="4853503">gumbyphv</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;I found BCP263 Edmonton (Ravine Drive).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mrs. Gumby had found out yesterday that she had an unexpected day off today so she decided to come up to Edmonton with me.  After the CITO event I dropped her off at West Ed to spend a few hours with a friend of hers and I took that opportunity to try and find as many caps as I could before she had to be back in Red Deer.  I parked on the street and made the nice short walk over to the cap.  Checked near the tree and there was the nicely exposed cap.  Another great cap with a great view.  TFTBC  &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
